From b089768a11ad54ebd88dd38db413f82f7e7617e9 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Christopher Owen <3221756+christopherowen@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 17 Oct 2026 02:52:44 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 150/274] Kernel preparation: owners declare from a walk of the
 loaded model; TileLang linear methods declare, bind and warm

prepare.declare(calls, bind, warm): calls() lists an owner's own TileLang calls
(compiled in one pool), warm() runs kernels whose keys their library computes
(TileKernels) on placeholder inputs, bind() stores the owner's kernels after the
cache freezes. The worker lets every module (declare_kernels) and every
module's linear method (declare_layer_kernels) declare after loading, since
methods are often attached after a layer is built.

The block-32 FP8, BF16, scaled and split linear methods declare their GEMMs
from the same key tables their binds use and warm TileKernels' per-token cast
for each small-batch bucket they can launch; weight processing keeps only the
scale words and the power-of-two fold.

